// The Go workspace: the three modules under apps/, and nothing else.
//
// `go.work` exists here for one reason, and it is not convenience. Each
// module has its own import path, so `apps/dataplane` cannot import
// `apps/console-api/internal/...` — Go's internal rule already forbids it
// across modules — and neither module's go.mod may require the other. The
// workspace is what lets a developer run `go build ./...` and `go test ./...`
// from an application directory without `go mod tidy` reaching for a sibling;
// the boundary itself is enforced by the module paths, not by this file.
//
// It is committed on purpose. A workspace file is local state by default and
// belongs in .gitignore when it only wires up a developer's machine; this one
// states a repository-wide invariant, and CI runs the same commands a
// contributor does against it. Should `go work sync` ever need checksums
// beyond the modules' own go.sum files it writes `go.work.sum` beside this
// file — that one is committed on the same terms, and the Go tasks in each
// `moon.yml` already name it as an input.
go 1.26

use (
	./apps/console-api
	./apps/dataplane
	./apps/dataplane-api
)
